AP Reelume (the "Program") is owned by AP Solutions. This licence describes what
you may and may not do with it. By installing, copying or using the Program you
accept these terms. If you do not accept them, do not install or use it.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

AP Solutions grants you a free of charge, worldwide, non-exclusive,
non-transferable and revocable right to:

  1.1 Install and use the Program on as many devices as you wish, at no cost and
      with no time limit.
  1.2 Use it for any purpose, personal or professional, including the commercial
      activity of the person using it.
  1.3 Make backup copies of the installer for your own use.
  1.4 Read the source code wherever AP Solutions publishes it, for the sole
      purpose of examining it, auditing its behaviour and checking what the
      Program claims about itself.
  1.5 Build the source code yourself, for yourself and without modifying it, for
      the sole purpose of checking that the program AP Solutions distributes
      corresponds to the published source. The result of that build is for your
      personal use and remains subject to this licence.

There is nothing to pay, no registration and no account.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Except where applicable law expressly permits it notwithstanding this licence,
you may not:

  2.1 Modify the Program, its source code or its binaries, or create derivative
      works of it.
  2.2 Redistribute it: publish, share, host, package or hand it to third parties,
      whether free of charge or for a fee, in whole or in part.
  2.3 Sell, rent, assign, lend or sublicense it, or offer it as a service.
  2.4 Decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer it, except to the extent
      mandatory law allows.
  2.5 Remove or alter copyright, licence or attribution notices, or the marks.
  2.6 Use the names "AP Reelume" or "AP Solutions", or their logos, to identify
      or promote any other product or service.

As an exception to 2.1, 2.4 and clause 3, you may modify the Program for your
own use, in order to use it with a modified version of the libraries that
clause 4 identifies as under LGPL licences, and reverse engineer it to debug
those modifications. This exception does not entitle you to redistribute the
modified Program.

Publishing the source code grants you no rights over it. Being able to read it
does not entitle you to copy it, reuse it or incorporate it into any other work.

3. OWNERSHIP

The Program is licensed, not sold. AP Solutions retains ownership and all
intellectual property rights in it, including those this licence does not
expressly mention. Only AP Solutions may modify the Program, and only AP
Solutions decides whether it is commercialised and on what terms.

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Program incorporates third-party components governed by their own licences,
which prevail over this one in everything concerning those components. The
inventory of those components, the licence of each and the full text of each
licence travel inside the package, in the `licenses/` folder, and are listed in
the NOTICE file.

Nothing in this licence limits, or is intended to limit, the rights those
third-party licences grant you over those components.

5. THE PUBLIC REPOSITORY, AND WHAT IT GRANTS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

AP Solutions publishes the Program's source code in a public repository hosted by
a third party (the "Platform"), for two purposes: so that anyone may examine it,
and so that the project's build and verification machines can work on it.

The Platform's terms of service grant its users, of their own force and
